on friday former presidential candidate  hillary clinton spoke at bloomberg's new  economic forum in singapore she  specifically called out things like  disinformation and artificial  intelligence as things to worry about  moving forward in the future but one of  the things that caught everyone's eye  was also comments around  cryptocurrencies she said quote what  looks like a very interesting and  somewhat exotic effort to literally mine  new coins in order to trade with them  has the potential to undermining  currencies for undermining the role of  the dollar as a reserve currency for  destabilizing nations perhaps starting  with small ones but going much much  larger she explicitly is laying out that  bitcoin and cryptocurrencies are  inherently opposed to other types of  fiat currencies there are central bank  currencies that exist in the world today  i don't necessarily agree with that  there's a strong argument that i've  talked with people like microstrategy  ceo michael saylor that actually the  dollar is going to get stronger and  stronger at the exact same time that  bitcoin continues to gain adoption as  well what would that world look like  well what you would see is bitcoin  rising and continuing to be seen as a  decentralized digital global store of  value it simply would allow people to  convert any asset into bitcoin and hold  it and not be debased by any government  or central bank around the world that  store a value would preserve purchasing  power and it would increase over a long  period of time as long as demand  continued to increase but at the same  time that the global store value was  rising in prominence and gaining  adoption the u.s dollar would continue  to benefit from the collapse of  developing nation currencies as well why  well in the united states as an example  there is a tax regime that makes it very  very difficult to spend bitcoin every  time that you spend bitcoin you are  faced with capital gains taxation and so  there's a financial incentive to simply  hold the asset we know that 70 to 80 of  bitcoin is held illiquid right now  depending on how you count that  illiquidity and so ultimately what we  are watching is lots and lots of weak  fiat currencies continue to fail and  everyone around the world wants dollars  they like the idea of the stability of  the dollar the faith and credit of the  united states and so there's a world in  the future of coexistence between the  dollar and bitcoin where bitcoin serves  as the global store of value and which  is the click of a button you can convert  back and forth between dollars and  bitcoin and anytime you actually go to  spend your currency will be in dollars  the medium of exchange and so in that  world bitcoin would rise to more and  more prominence it would gain larger and  larger market share but also the dollar  would do the same and so if that was to  happen these comments around  destabilizing nations or in undermining  a reserve currency would not necessarily  be true instead what we would see is we  would see more adoption of a global  store of value it would eat into things  like real estate or fine art or other  types of store value assets but it  wouldn't necessarily eat into the dollar  being used as a medium of exchange it's  a very interesting way to look at it  it's at direct odds with the way that  hillary clinton is talking about it in  terms of her speech at the bloomberg new  economy forum in singapore on friday i  also think that there is a very deep  peace that people need to pay attention  to which is that there are lots and lots  of people who are very prominent or  experts or have tons of experience in  other areas of the world but they're not  necessarily experts on this specific  type of technology and so we have to  remember that no matter how smart you  are no matter what you've accomplished  in the past if you have not spent the  time if you've not spent hundreds if not  thousands of hours studying bitcoin and  cryptocurrencies then we have to take  their opinions with a grain of salt so  ultimately what i think will continue to  occur and what i have the highest  conviction is that bitcoin itself will  continue to rise as a global store value  the decentralized digital asset will  continue to be adopted by millions and  millions of people around the world  whether it's individuals corporations  financial institutions or nation states  like el salvador people will realize  that having a digital private property  in bitcoin where you can hold your  private keys you can store value in a  place where no one can debase it no one  can confiscate it and no one can censor  your transactions that is going to be  very very attractive in the future so we  appreciate what other people are saying  but remember bitcoin is a digital store  of value is just getting started in my  opinion
 

